\section*{Correlation cancellation for multiplicative functions}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 007; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that ordinary two-point Liouville averages have a logarithmic power saving on fixed nonproportional affine forms, and bounded multiplicative functions satisfy the corrected binary Elliott assertion under uniform nonpretentiousness.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
For Liouville $\lambda(n)=(-1)^{\Omega(n)}$, there is claimed an absolute $c>0$ such that every fixed $a_1,a_2\ge1$, $b_1,b_2\ge0$ with $a_1b_2-a_2b_1\ne0$ has a constant $C$ satisfying
\[
 |\sum_{n\le X}\lambda(a_1n+b_1)\lambda(a_2n+b_2)|\le C X/(\log X)^c\quad(X\ge3).
\]
The coefficients need not be coprime, but are fixed as $X$ grows. A second claim concerns multiplicative $f_1,f_2:\mathbb N\to\{z:|z|\le1\}$, at least one satisfying, for every fixed Dirichlet character $\chi$,
\[
 \inf_{|t|\le N}\left(\sum_{p\le N}\frac{1-\operatorname{Re}(f(p)\overline{\chi(p)p^{it}})}p\right)^{1/2}\longrightarrow\infty.
\]
For any distinct fixed nonnegative $h_1,h_2$ the claimed ordinary, rather than logarithmically weighted, conclusion is
\[
 N^{-1}\sum_{n=1}^Nf_1(n+h_1)f_2(n+h_2)\longrightarrow0.
\]

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 007; 2026-09-24), centering decomposes the correlation into graph and rough-number contributions. Short-interval cancellation controls a Fourier multiplier, while a conditioned finite-cylinder sieve extracts enough graph constraints to contradict a persistent bias.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The binary Elliott conclusion assumes unit-disc multiplicative functions and nonpretentiousness uniform over the growing frequency range. This record permits unbounded factors or only pointwise twist divergence, and also includes higher-order correlations. Those hypotheses and extra factors are outside the claimed theorem.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 007; 2026-09-24), OpenAI lists Lean statements for this assertion: ordinary two-point Liouville averages have a logarithmic power saving on fixed nonproportional affine forms, and bounded multiplicative functions satisfy the corrected binary Elliott assertion under uniform nonpretentiousness.

This coverage does not establish a formal proof of the complete problem as stated here.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{OrdinaryElliott.lean}, \texttt{OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.OrdinaryCorrelations.binary\_corrected\_elliott}, \texttt{OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.affine\_corrected\_elliott}, \texttt{OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.binary\_corrected\_elliott}, \texttt{OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.liouville\_log\_saving}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

